From a1943428bef2b40b09d7f1ce5ee60ae1039be10f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: djnice <djnice@freemail.hu>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:12:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] AML: put the video layer into screenshots

The Amlogic video layer never reaches the framebuffer, so screenshots held the
GUI only (the video area black) and video captures (TakeScreenshot(video),
render captures) always failed: CScreenshotAML was no longer called anywhere.

- CScreenshotSurfaceAML reads the GUI like the GLES surface and puts the video
  picture under it where the GUI is not opaque (premultiplied over the
  transparent clear), at the video destination rectangle the renderer
  publishes; RGBA, BGRA, X2BGR10 and RGBA64 readbacks are handled.
- CRendererAML::CaptureVideoFrame serves video captures as BGRA.
- The picture is read with CAP_FLAG_AT_CURRENT: no wait for the next frame,
  so it works while paused and does not hold the render thread for seconds.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
